[1m== Step 2 of 3 - the foreman[0m
[90m  The foreman plans the work and decides what happens when a task needs[0m
[90m  judgment. It runs whenever work finishes, so it uses that agent's quota.[0m
[90m  Only claude and codex can be the foreman; it uses the model picked above[0m
[90m  and its effort.[0m
>  [36m 1[0m  [1mclaude/sonnet[0m
   [36m 2[0m  codex/gpt-6.1-sol
[1m  Pick 1-2 [0m[36m[1][0m[1m:[0m

  [90m-> change later: brigada project foreman --harness H --model M[0m

[1m== Step 3 of 3 - how brigada tests the work[0m
[90m  When an agent finishes a task, brigada runs one command in that task's[0m
[90m  own copy of the repo (never in your working copy):[0m
[90m    passes (exit 0)  the work goes on to review by another model family[0m
[90m    fails            the work goes back to the agent, with the output[0m
[90m  Use the command you run yourself to be sure nothing broke: tests,[0m
[90m  lint, type checks. Claude workers may run it too before handing in.[0m

  Found in this repo:
>   [36m 1[0m  [1muv run pytest[0m  [90mpytest, from uv.lock[0m
[1m  Pick 1, or type a command [0m[36m[1][0m[1m:[0m

  [90m-> change later: .brigada/project.yaml: default_check; brigada project import[0m

Plan
  Agents:
    claude    sonnet (default)                   Anthropic    writes code, reviews
    codex     gpt-6.1-sol (default)              OpenAI       writes code, reviews
    kimi      kimi-code/k3 (default)             Moonshot     reviews only
    opencode  zai-coding-plan/glm-5.3 (default)  Zhipu (GLM)  writes code, reviews
  Reviews: 4 model families, so every task can get a reviewer of another one.
  Foreman: claude/sonnet
  Check: uv run pytest (init doesn't run it; change it later in .brigada/project.yaml)
  What workers may do:
    claude    edit files; run only: uv run pytest
    codex     edit files and run commands inside codex's sandbox
    opencode  edit files; no commands
  Files in this repository (brigada never commits them):
    .brigada/project.yaml                    new  the settings above
    .mcp.json                                new  lets Claude Code here use brigada (Claude Code
                                                  asks you to approve it)
    .claude/settings.local.json              new  private, kept out of git: when your Claude turn
                                                  ends, brigada's foreman picks up what happened
                                                  meanwhile
    .claude/skills/brigada-foreman/SKILL.md  new  rules for your Claude session
    (show full contents: --verbose)
  Codex, optional: to plan from your own Codex session, run once yourself:
    codex mcp add brigada-foreman -- brigada mcp --foreman
  In the background: a runner starts now and keeps going (log: ~/.local/state/brigada/runner.log;
    stop it with: brigada stop). The engine starts when needed and stops after 30 idle minutes.

To change later: brigada init (agents, models, effort),
  brigada project foreman (foreman), .brigada/project.yaml (check),
  brigada config (see everything).

